      "message": "feat(fixtures): edit and re-fit a placed mod vise pair\n\nSetModJaw changes a placed jaw block's figures (or slide) and regenerates\nits solid through UpdateModel, as SetVise does; RefitModVise re-fits the\nadjustable block to the stock as it stands (re-picks its hole and slide by\nthe placing fit). One undo step each, refusals by name. MCP tools\nset_mod_jaw and refit_mod_vise; the jaw block row gets \"Edit jaw block…\"\nand \"Re-fit to stock\".\n\n#833 review hardening: a jaw that was not in front of the stock before a\nplate edit is judged clear, so an edit that brings it 16 mm into the\nstock is refused (judge_face, shared with SetModJaw); mcp_plate pins the\nwarning field of set_fixture_plate.\n\nThe dual-station block is held back (one stock per setup, fixtures judged\nper setup - see docs/decisions/832-mod-vise-edit-refit.md).\n\nRefs #832\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
